  "body": "# Description\n\nWhen a module raises during CUDA graph warmup, temporary discovery hooks and capture-owned state can survive the exception. Retrying capture on the same module can then run with stale hooks or wrappers. Remove owned hooks in `finally` and restore saved RNG state, module class calls, FP8 tensors and the capture flag before propagating the exception.\n\nThis is an independent dependency fix for [Megatron FSDP v2 partial graph validation](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/issues/9113). It does not add scheduler or communication behavior, or make fatal CUDA errors recoverable.\n\n## Type of change\n\n- [x] Bug fix\n\n## Changes\n\n- Clean up temporary warmup forward hooks even when discovery forward raises.\n- Restore the existing saved state in an outer `finally`; preserve successful-path behavior.\n- Add a BF16 Linear/dropout failure–retry regression checking hook/class/RNG/capture-state restoration, then exact output and parameter-gradient parity with an eager copy. Document the recovery boundary.\n\n## Validation\n\nRTX A6000, PyTorch 2.11.0+cu130, installed TE 2.20.2 native binaries. Stock 2.20.2 reproduces the leftover-hook failure. An isolated overlay with equivalent release cleanup passes two focused checks. The patched upstream-main Python module passes three focused checks: failure/retry, owned parameter gradients and skipping returned-gradient cloning. Final code differs from the tested Python module only by documentation.\n\nDownstream two-rank GPT and Hybrid MoE tests inject a failure after an actual QKV forward, retry capture and match eager training state; both pass on each rank. Shared installed TE is unchanged. Formatting, targeted pylint, diff whitespace and license checks pass; pylint reports an existing config/version warning. A PyTorch AccumulateGrad stream warning is also present in the healthy stock control. No warning suppression was added. Full L0 suites and a current-main native rebuild remain pending.\n\n[Commands, overlay hashes and per-rank logs](https://github.com/WEIXILIN0307/Megatron-LM/tree/c8883d7b176494c59a7f32ef585f655471bcff11/mfsdp-v2-core-split-20261112/gap-closure-20261113).\n\n# Checklist\n\n- [x] Read the contributing guidelines.\n- [x] Add focused regression coverage and document the recovery boundary.\n- [x] Run the selected regression and downstream composition checks.\n- [ ] Run full upstream L0/CI.\n- [ ] Human author review before marking ready for maintainer review.\n\n",
